{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":222872,"duration_api_ms":219596,"num_turns":30,"result":"","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"373db8be-0a37-491b-ba93-e65f5090fe82","total_cost_usd":1.5624375000000001,"usage":{"input_tokens":22,"cache_creation_input_tokens":97900,"cache_read_input_tokens":1531005,"output_tokens":7398,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":97900,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":22,"outputTokens":7398,"cacheReadInputTokens":1531005,"cacheCreationInputTokens":97900,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":1.5624375000000001,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"summary":"Reviewed all 22 changed files covering: ConcentrationView struct and helpers on WaterState/TankState, legacy_total_param_to_mg_per_l conversion for kinetic parameters, concentration-based Monod refactoring in nitrogen_cycle.rs/plant_growth.rs/algae_growth.rs, schema v2→v3 migration, API handler migration support, weighted plant limitation factor, tests, and documentation updates. Tests all pass. One significant correctness bug found in the plant substrate limitation factor, plus a minor robustness gap.","amendments":[{"body":"Fix dimensional mismatch in plant substrate limitation factors at plant_growth.rs:60-61. `substrate_n_factor = half_saturation(substrate_n, plant_half_saturation_n_mg_n_per_l)` passes raw mg totals from `total_substrate_n()` (e.g. 40 mg) against a concentration-based half-saturation constant (e.g. 0.4 mg/L after legacy_total_param_to_mg_per_l divides by 20). This makes `half_saturation(40, 0.4) ≈ 0.99`, rendering substrate limitation essentially non-functional regardless of actual nutrient depletion. Same issue for substrate_p_factor. Either (a) convert substrate totals to a per-area or per-volume density before passing to half_saturation, or (b) use the original total-based half-saturation constant for the substrate compartment while reserving the concentration-based constant for water-column terms.","rationale":"This is a correctness regression introduced by the refactor. The old code was dimensionally consistent (both accessible_n and half-sat were in mg total). The new code correctly converts water-column terms to mg/L but leaves substrate totals in mg while the half-saturation constant has been converted to mg/L. The existing volume-invariance test does not catch this because it sets substrate_uptake_bias=0 and clears substrate layers."},{"body":"Add a test for plant substrate limitation that verifies substrate depletion actually reduces the limitation factor. The existing test `plant_water_column_limitation_is_volume_invariant_at_fixed_concentration` explicitly zeroes out substrate bias (`substrate_uptake_bias: Some(0.0)`) and clears substrate layers, so it cannot catch the dimensional mismatch in the substrate half-saturation path. A test with nonzero substrate bias and varying substrate nutrient levels would catch this class of bug.","rationale":"The dimensional mismatch bug went undetected because no test exercises the substrate limitation path. A test that sets substrate_uptake_bias > 0 and checks that low substrate nutrients actually reduce growth would provide coverage for this critical path."}]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"f5b2759d-235b-4716-87be-ce2146e64eb4"}
